<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Passarowitz</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1718</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Peace of Passarowitz · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-turkish-war-1716-1718">Austro-Turkish War (1716–1718)</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Passarowitz was signed on 21 July 1718 at Passarowitz, now Požarevac in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a>, between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> on one side and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> monarchy and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> on the other. It ended the Austro-Turkish war of 1716 to 1718 and the Ottoman–Venetian war begun in 1714. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> gained the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banat">Banat</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timisoara">Temeswar</a>, northern Serbia with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgrade">Belgrade</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oltenia">Oltenia</a>, while Venice lost the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Morea</a> but kept its gains in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dalmatia">Dalmatia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-passarowitz.jpg" alt="Treaty of Passarowitz" width="320" height="412" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: WikiEditor2004 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tamis_banat1718_1739.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
